## 3) Design goals for low latency and scaling

### Low-latency principles
- Keep the hot path in-memory
- Avoid blocking I/O in strategy/execution path
- Use preallocated buffers where possible
- Minimize object allocations
- Prefer lock-free or single-threaded event loops per shard
- Use binary protocols when possible

### Scaling principles
- Separate hot path from slow path
- Partition by symbol, strategy, or venue
- Make services stateless where possible
- Use message queues or streaming only at boundaries
- Persist asynchronously

