## One important fix
The implementation above is a good starting point, but for cleaner correctness, you may want to slightly simplify the initialization logic so the first tick is always inserted and later ticks always update.

Here is a more correct `run` loop:

```rust
pub async fn run(
    mut input_rx: mpsc::Receiver<MarketTick>,
    aggregate_tx: broadcast::Sender<PriceAggregate>,
) {
    let mut state: HashMap<String, PriceAggregate> = HashMap::new();

    while let Some(tick) = input_rx.recv().await {
        let agg = state.entry(tick.symbol.clone()).or_insert_with(|| {
            PriceAggregate::new(tick.symbol.clone(), tick.price, tick.timestamp_ms)
        });

        if agg.count == 1 && agg.last_price == tick.price && agg.updated_at_ms == tick.timestamp_ms {
            // first observation already captured by new()
        } else {
            agg.update(tick.price, tick.timestamp_ms);
        }

        let _ = aggregate_tx.send(agg.clone());
    }
}
```

