## Why this is memory-efficient

- Uses `BufReader` to reduce syscalls.
- Reads one line at a time.
- Reuses a single `String` buffer.
- Borrows fields from the line buffer instead of allocating new `String`s.
- Avoids loading the whole file into memory.

